course: dictionary
lesson: 11076
title: Welding: joining metal with heat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Welding is a way of joining two pieces of metal, or plastic, into one piece. You heat the edges until they melt a little and flow together, then they cool and harden. The sentence «Robot arms join the steel pieces with several thousand spot welds» tells you that welding joins things, and the many small joins hold the car together.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Welding light can hurt eyes» tells you that welding makes a very bright light. «So welding happens behind screens» tells you that people are kept safe from that light. Ask yourself: what would the sentence mean if welding did not make a bright light?
explain: Welding is also a verb. Weld is the base word, and welds, welded and welding are its other forms. «He is welding the gate» means he is joining the gate by heating it now. A welder is a person whose job is welding.
fact: Welding means joining two pieces of metal by heating them until they melt a little and flow together.
fact: When the melted metal cools, it hardens into one piece.
fact: Welding is also the -ing form of weld: «He is welding the gate.»
fact: Welding makes very bright light and sparks, so welders wear a dark mask, gloves and thick clothes.
fact: «Welding torch» and «welding mask» are useful phrases, and «weld together» means to join things by welding.
exercise: «Robot arms join the steel pieces with several thousand spot welds.» What does welding do to the metal? | Cuts it into small bits | *Heats it until it melts a little and flows together | Freezes it solid | Paints it bright red
exercise: «Welding light can hurt eyes, so welding happens behind screens.» Why do welders work behind screens? | To hide the car from view | To make the metal cool faster | To keep the robots warm | *To protect people's eyes from the bright light
exercise: «He is welding the gate.» Which word is the -ing form of weld? | welded | welder | welds | *welding
test: A welder says, «My job is welding.» What is a welder? | A tool for cutting paper | A type of car engine | *A person whose job is welding | A kind of bright lamp
test: Which everyday thing might have been joined by welding? | A bowl of soup | *A steel bridge | A woolly hat | A paper aeroplane
exam: Why must welders never look straight at the flash, and what does this tell you about welding? | It is too dark to see the metal | It makes the gloves wet | *It is very bright and can hurt the eyes, so welders wear a dark mask | It makes the metal smell bad
